lse,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310664,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA2NjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:input","name":"topic:input","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-04-12T19:11:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-07T14:09:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4.1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - AMD Ryzen 9 5900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\n\n\nI have `Scene1 `→ `Scene2 `→ `Scene3 `for android. **Other scenes are all .free() after loading a scene**, so not in tree\n Scene2 and Scene3 have function below:\n\n```\nfunc _notification(what):\n\tif what == NOTIFICATION_WM_GO_BACK_REQUEST:\n\t\t_on_back_scn_btn_pressed()\n```\n\nThe problem is when i press back button **one time** on Scene3, Scene2’s above method is also triggered which causes Scene3 to go to Scene1 in one press. So shortly **in one press** new loaded scene's notification can also be triggered which causes multiple \"**backs**\". \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nMake 3 scenes and middle scene should be loaded fast. Scene2 and Scene3 should have a method like above. \n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n-","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105324/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"h